 is more by the way  than the european union it's more than  the united states so those assets have  been frozen for some time now well let's  talk specifically about chelsea first  and foremost you're not a fan are you  i'm a palace fan okay fair enough fair  enough so apologies if a suitable buyer  for chelsea was found is the government  currently minded to allow that deal to  go through yeah so as the license  conditions are written today  the sale would not be allowed however if  a buyer emerged then it would be open to  that buyer or to the football club  to approach the government and ask for  the license conditions to be varied in a  way that allowed that sale to take place  so they'd be they'd be able to approach  the government to make a proposal  but to be clear  no proposal would be accepted which saw  the money the proceeds of any sale  ending up in  an unrestricted bank account owned by  abramovic he can't benefit from the  proceeds of any sale let's talk a little  bit then about about the the ukrainian  refugee crisis and and clearly as a  crisis estimates originally were around  about 2 million people may well be  leaving the country those look to be  doubled the british public is going to  be asked to take in in refugees  themselves just explain a little bit  more about that scheme well it's worth  just talking about the the full spectrum  of our response to the humanitarian  crisis and first of all we've donated  aid uh valued at over 400 million pounds  to help the humanitarian crisis on the  ukrainian border that's more than any  other country in the world and that is  the that is the response that the  ukrainian president principally asked  for and we've met that we've done it  more than any other country  secondly there is a route for fam people  with family members extended family  members in the uk to come over here and  the home secretary announced just  yesterday that where people have family  here and have a ukrainian passport then  we're 